<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">British Windward Islands</h1><p class="st-meta">1833 CE – 1960 CE · capital Bridgetown; later St George's</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Grouping of Britain's southern Caribbean islands under one governor from 1833 to 1960, linking Grenada, Saint Vincent, Saint Lucia and later Dominica.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1833 the British government placed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/barbados">Barbados</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/grenada">Grenada</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-vincent-island">Saint Vincent</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tobago">Tobago</a> under a single governor-in-chief resident in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bridgetown">Bridgetown</a>, to cut costs and coordinate the transition from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saint-lucia">Saint Lucia</a> was added in 1838.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/windward-islands">Windward Islands</a> was an administrative union rather than a federation: each island kept its own laws, treasury and, at first, assembly, under a lieutenant governor or administrator. Most islands became crown colonies in the 1870s. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/barbados">Barbados</a> resisted plans for closer union, and riots in 1876 led to its withdrawal in 1885, after which the governor resided at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-georges-grenada">St George's</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/grenada">Grenada</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tobago">Tobago</a> left for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinidad">Trinidad</a> in 1889, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commonwealth-of-dominica">Dominica</a> joined from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leeward-islands">Leeward Islands</a> in 1940.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The member islands entered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/west-indies-federation">West Indies Federation</a> in 1958, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/windward-islands">Windward Islands</a> governorship was abolished in 1960. Its members later became independent as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/grenada">Grenada</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saint-vincent-and-the-grenadines">Saint Vincent and the Grenadines</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saint-lucia">Saint Lucia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commonwealth-of-dominica">Dominica</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/british-windward-islands.jpg" alt="British Windward Islands" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_British_Windward_Islands_(1953%E2%80%931958).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1833 CE – 1960 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bridgetown; later St George's</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anglicanism and Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English and French Creole</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/grenada">Grenada</a>, <a href="/countries/saint-vincent-and-the-grenadines">Saint Vincent and the Grenadines</a>, <a href="/countries/saint-lucia">Saint Lucia</a>, <a href="/countries/dominica">Dominica</a>, <a href="/countries/barbados">Barbados</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Windward Islands colony</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1896&amp;focus=british-windward-islands" aria-label="British Windward Islands on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3045 1690 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where British Windward Islands lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3365 1946L3365 1946M3365 1946L4997 651M3365 1946L3303 1984M3365 1946L3321 1944M3365 1946L3324 1865M3365 1946L3330 1912"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3365 1946h0M4997 651h0M3303 1984h0M3321 1944h0M3324